t  which holds the lion's share of voting  power he used that position to appoint a  new board with some allies to tilt the  balance of power in his favor his mother  and his sisters say this other board is  illegitimate it's going to be up to bc  supreme court to decide who's in the  right legally i've been speaking to  corporate governance experts legal  experts they say it's just a matter of  time though before edward prevails  i'm not sure how they're going to uh  win i mean they may get it delayed  saying okay you did it wrong  procedurally mr rogers you should have  done it not by a private note you should  have gone to a formal shareholder  meeting but that doesn't diminish or  remove his authority  to vote those shares if i was a betting  person i think edward is going to win in  court today but what happens after that  is is up for debate  so anne where does this go from here  well regardless of what's decided by  bc's top court keep in mind both sides  have deep pockets and they have the  ability to drag this out and appeal all  of this is happening while regulators  decide whether or not to green light the  rogers take over that 26 billion dollar  deal of shaw which would be its biggest  acquisition ever perhaps it's most  important robin all right and gaviola in  toronto  still ahead why tens of thousands were  locked down in the happiest place on  earth  today there were tears of joy at  airports in australia after more than 18  months the country has finally relaxed  its international border restrictions  for now travel is limited to fully  vaccinated australian citizens permanent  residents and their immediate families  international tourists could be allowed  sometime next year  in china a single case of kova 19 has  shut down shanghai disneyland according  to chinese state media officials sealed  off the theme park yesterday after  learning a woman in the area had tested  positive public health teams entered the  park in full hazmat suits and the nearly  34 thousand people inside had to be  tested before leaving  officials say all tests came back  negative  the world has hit yet another grim  milestone in the pandemic the number of  people killed by the virus has now  officially surpassed 5 million and those  are just the confirmed deaths experts  say the true number is likely much  higher the united states has recorded  the most deaths of any country more than  740 thousand brazil is second hardest  hit with more than 600 000 deaths  up next how this year's silvercross  mother is honoring her daughter's  sacrifice  every year the royal canadian legion  picks a silver cross mother on  remembrance day she lays a wreath on  behalf of all mothers who lost a son or  daughter in military service it's an  immense honor but one no parent wants a  woman from quebec is this year's silver  cross mother her daughter corporal karen  black was only 21 years old when she was  killed in afghanistan mike armstrong has  her story  the small village of les meschen quebec  is tucked away on the south shore of the  saint lawrence river it is a world away  from afghanistan but not so far that in  april of 2009  they couldn't hear the bagpipes  [Applause]  when corporal kerenble was carried up  the ramp by her brothers and sisters in  arms in kandahar her mother says the  village changed  she says the war seemed very close to  everyone in les misery it was no longer  just something on tv  jose simal still lives on the banks of a  small creek where she raised her two  children her son billy was just 14 when  kevin was killed walk around her home  and there are memories of karen in every  direction a photo is a member of the  12th armored regiment a picture in  civilian clothes  and the one she was given on this day by  the governor general when karen's body  arrived back in canada at trenton  it hangs in the kitchen  every time i turn my head she's beside  me sima says she is everywhere in my  house  corporal karen blair was killed april 13  2009. she was driving a coyote an  armored vehicle part of the patrol just  meant to show canadian forces were  present they were north of kandahar when  they hit an ied play was killed four men  were injured and everyone involved was  affected they'd been in afghanistan  barely two weeks  simal says every year around november 11  men and women who were with karen come  to visit some are still serving some  have left the military but it's a time  when they want to be together  now simar won't be home this remembrance  day she'll be serving as the silver  cross mother in ottawa she's been asked  before but chose to spend the day with  keren's friends  the only one she missed was in 2010 when  simal went to afghanistan herself on a  next of kin visit  small says she wanted to breathe the  same air where karen took her last  breath and to see the country she was  trying to help  now it has been difficult over the last  few months watching what's happened in  afghanistan the taliban again taking  control of the country small says she  focuses on what was accomplished how a  generation of women went to school and  were educated  and how some are pushing back  canada she says made a difference  karen didn't die for  nothing now her daughter knew every  corner of the village but there have  been some changes there's a street named  corporal kerenble  and a monument that went up just a  couple of years after she was  lost says she sees her daughter every  day while she used to babysit children  in the village she now watches over  everyone  mike armstrong global news les meschens  quebec  a beautiful story mike global news will  have live coverage of the remembrance  day ceremony in ottawa you can watch it  at 10 30 a.m eastern 7 30 pacific we'll  also be streaming the special on our  website  globalnews.ca  and that is global national for this  monday night i'm robin gill tonight your  canada is this bear cub hanging out in  pork aquitlam bc we'd love to see your  corner of the country so please keep  sending your photos to viewers at  globalnational.com  thank you for watching and i'll see you  back here tomorrow have a great night  [Music]
 

